A||||7||thecage||rust proofing||||1||
Z||000000||thecage||11-15-2001||06:31 PM||||Does annual rustproofing (oil) help save the precious fiero from further rust or is it just a waste of money. Some thoughts on this subject will be appreciated. Like should i just do the undercarriage or the entire car. They want to drill holes in the rocker panels and door frames etc to apply this stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000001||thecage||11-15-2001||06:57 PM||||any comments?||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou||11-15-2001||07:09 PM|||| Fiero frames  were all dipped in a rust resistant coating at the factory.  Don't rust proff it!  The holes that they drill are where the rust will come from. This is what caused rusty jones ( a rust prevention company ) to go bankrupt , they had to pay all the claims for rust that started from the drill holes.  I know this from experience.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||11-15-2001||09:14 PM||||An annual oil spray type undercoating can't hurt.  My Samurais' all had a leaky valve cover and the spots it ran were the only places they didn't rust.<P>Don't let them drill holes.  You can pour creeping rust proofing into the doors with the inner panel off.  Make sure any drains are kept clear, tho.<P>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||11-15-2001||11:22 PM||||you're kidding...right?  your car is plastic.||||reg||5
Z||000005||thecage||11-15-2001||11:49 PM||||thanks for all the comment's. Even though I will not drive it in the winter, I'm going to get the underbody sprayed with oil. I figure it can't hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-15-2001||11:50 PM||||just rustproof the stuff that usually rusts yourself. Buy the rubberized undercoat spray cans. the floor pans, rear trunk pan, battery, strut tower areas are all that really need it. Why would you drill holes in plastic rocker panels. they rivet on, no metal in them. Should tell you they dont know what there doing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||11-16-2001||06:42 AM||||Good one Tom.   If you drive your car long enough in Canada, yes your Fiero will be all plastic (+ some glass).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>The idea of the galvanized coating is that the coating sacrifices itself to rust instead of the metal frame, etc.  It doesn't seal out rust.<P>The oil will be fine.  There are 'rocker' panels under the plastic and the area around where the the cooling tubes run is rusty on a lot of CDN cars.<P>Gary||||reg||6
